Dan McGuirk schrieb:
> 
> A.V. de Vet wrote:
> 
> > What are the odds of a random generated monster
> > carrying a wand of wishing? Or a magic marker?
> 
> I'm pretty sure they are zero; i.e., monsters are never generated
> carrying such items.

This isn't the case. Monsters have a _small_ chance of carrying a
random item of treasure which can be just about anything. Magic
markers definitely can be got off monsters, but i've yet to see a wand
of wishing created in a monster's inventory.

What the chances are i do not know, but they are rather small and i
_think_ monster level factors into it. A full-scale extinction seems
to net two or three magic markers, so don't count on it.

> > And, I might go crazy, is a Valk Extinctionist viable?
> 
> Yes, any class can be an extinctionist.  It's helpful if you can cast
> the create monster spell decently, which I've been able to do before as
> a Valkyrie.

It's even more helpful if you can recover spell points at a halfway
decent rate, which requires either the Eye of the Aethiopica or the
Mitre of Holiness (priest quest artefact); with the Mitre, it already
gets annoyingly slow. Without either, i expect it would require
superhuman patience.

